WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.730 --> 00:00:05.060
The hatchet has been buried, and this "Fast
and Furious" cast member is roaring back into

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:05.742
the race.

00:00:05.742 --> 00:00:09.830
Dwayne Johnson is set to headline his very
own "Fast and Furious" film.

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:14.019
Audiences for "Fast X" were delighted to find
out that the film's mid-credits scene features

00:00:14.019 --> 00:00:15.480
the return of Luke Hobbs.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:19.619
This brief cameo came after Johnson publically
made it clear that he wouldn't be returning

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:21.310
to the billion-dollar franchise.

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:25.520
Now, The Hollywood Reporter confirms that
Johnson is on track to return for a brand

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:30.323
new "Fast" project, which will center Hobbs
and various other "Furious" characters.

00:00:30.323 --> 00:00:32.031
"Why do I smell baby oil?"

00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:34.850
"You keep running your pie hole, you're gonna
smell an ass-kicking."

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:39.550
The outlet notes that this isn't a sequel
to 2019's "Hobbs and Shaw," the first spin-off

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:40.980
in the "Fast" franchise.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:46.875
The Johnson-led project also isn't "Fast 11,"
which Louis Leterrier is expected to direct.

00:00:46.875 --> 00:00:50.688
Instead, insiders are describing it as "Fast
X.5."

00:00:50.688 --> 00:00:55.410
Is it an entry set directly after the events
of "Fast X," which saw the Fast Fam going

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:58.079
up against their number one hater Dante Reyes?

00:00:58.079 --> 00:01:02.270
Or is Johnson's latest "Furious" adventure
set to detail the operation he was leading

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:04.150
at the end of "Fast X"?

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:07.423
Only time will tell what Johnson and company
have in store for fans.

00:01:07.423 --> 00:01:11.572
One thing is certain: a core member of the
Fast family won't be showing up.

00:01:11.572 --> 00:01:15.780
While other actors from the franchise are
set to reprise their roles for Johnson's film,

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:20.000
the Hollywood Reporter says that Dominic Toretto
actor Vin Diesel won't be popping up.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.850
Diehard fans of the franchise will know that
Johnson and Diesel haven't been on the best

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:28.735
terms, which was one of the reasons why Johnson
was ready to leave Hobbs behind him and move on.

00:01:28.735 --> 00:01:33.430
Despite their public feud, Leterrier says
he helped convince Johnson to return to the

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:35.480
franchise with the "Fast X" mid-credits scene.

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:39.689
This time, it seems like Johnson and Diesel
have really moved on, ready to bring the Fast

00:01:39.689 --> 00:01:40.476
Fam together.

00:01:40.476 --> 00:01:43.829
Johnson said in a lengthy tweet following
the film's announcement,

00:01:43.829 --> 00:01:46.610
"Last summer Vin and I put all the past behind
us.

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:52.090
We'll lead with brotherhood and resolve – and
always take care of the franchise, characters

00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:53.090
&amp; FANS that we love."

00:01:53.317 --> 00:01:54.767
"Wasn't half bad having you work for me."

00:01:55.675 --> 00:02:00.315
[laughs]  "We all know you were working for me,
Hobbs."

00:02:00.315 --> 00:02:02.870
What compelled Johnson to return to the franchise?

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:07.320
In a video accompanying the tweet, Johnson
says that fan reactions to the character's

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:10.910
return made him realize it was time to return
to the franchise.

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:12.967
"You don't turn your back on family.

00:02:15.045 --> 00:02:16.545
Even if they do."

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:21.099
In his tweet, Dwayne Johnson teased that his
"Hobbs" movie, quote, "will serve as a fresh,

00:02:21.099 --> 00:02:24.530
new chapter &amp; set up for 'FASTX: Part II.'"

00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:29.691
Will this "fresh, new chapter" include an
appearance by Dante, who has a vendetta against Hobbs?

00:02:29.691 --> 00:02:34.960
While Johnson doesn't explicitly confirm Momoa's
return, he does say that, quote, "business

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:37.038
is about to pick up" between the two.

00:02:37.038 --> 00:02:38.732
"Daddy's gotta go to work."

00:02:38.732 --> 00:02:43.780
Ultimately, concrete details are slim on this
so-called "Fast X.5," though a writer has

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:46.110
been found in franchise OG Chris Morgan.

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:51.080
He's best known for penning some of the franchise's
most memorable films, including "Fast Five"

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:52.349
and "Tokyo Drift."

00:02:52.349 --> 00:02:57.030
Morgan also brought the "Hobbs &amp; Shaw" spin-off
to life, though he didn't return for "F9"

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:58.360
and "Fast X."

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:02.659
Some diehard "Fast" fans believe that Morgan
is the secret sauce to the franchise's success,

00:03:02.659 --> 00:03:06.573
so it's definitely exciting to see the screenwriter
return to the series.

00:03:06.573 --> 00:03:10.923
Johnson will also be producing his upcoming
"Fast and Furious" romp alongside Morgan.

00:03:11.139 --> 00:03:14.970
What's surprising is that they've found a
producing partner in Vin Diesel, signaling

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:17.227
that their feud has genuinely come to an end.

00:03:17.227 --> 00:03:19.830
That said, details are fairly scarce at the
moment.

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:24.230
A director isn't currently attached to the
project, and, according to Diesel, "Fast 11"

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:27.446
is set to race into cinemas in 2025.

00:03:27.446 --> 00:03:31.216
It remains to be seen if the Hobbs-centered
film will be released before that.

